Local modifications:
  - viz.html: the two CDN <script> tags (cytoscape from cdn.jsdelivr.net and
    marked from cdn.jsdelivr.net) were replaced, in the same position and
    order, with inline placeholder tokens:
        <script>/*__CYTOSCAPE_JS__*/</script>
        <script>/*__MARKED_JS__*/</script>
    so the libraries can be inlined at build time instead of fetched from a
    CDN. The pre-existing placeholder tokens /*__VIZ_CSS__*/, /*__VIZ_JS__*/,
    __BUNDLE_NAME__, and __BUNDLE_DATA__ were left untouched.
  - viz.js: no patch was needed. Markdown rendering already calls
    marked.parse(body, { breaks: false, gfm: true }), which is compatible
    with marked v13 UMD, so no marked(...) -> marked.parse(...) rewrite was
    applied.
  - These templates are consumed by a Node.js port, okf-graph.mjs, which
    also fixes bundle-absolute-link edge extraction and adds .mdx support
    (both differences from the upstream Python reference agent).
